# --- what belongs in this repository ----------------------------------------
#
# An allow-list of top-level DIRECTORIES, not a list of things to exclude. The reason is
# that the two failure modes are not symmetric. A directory forgotten here is simply
# absent from a clone and noticed the first time anyone builds; a run directory that slips
# in is 250 MB in the history, and history is only fixed by rewriting it.
#
# This file used to name each sandbox — claude-demo/, terror-report/, attn-article/,
# attn-v2/, RESULT/ — one line per live run someone happened to remember. That list grows
# every time the engine is validated on a new subject, and the cost of forgetting a line
# is paid once and permanently.
#
# Files in the root stay visible on purpose: they are few, they are all product
# (README, CLAUDE.md, pyproject.toml, uv.lock), and a new one is worth noticing in
# `git status` rather than hiding.
/*/
!/refract/
!/library/
!/tests/
!/examples/
!/web/
!/assets/
!/.claude/

# --- inside the allowed directories -----------------------------------------
#
# Run output is never product, wherever it appears — including under examples/, where a
# developer's own run would otherwise land in the index.
runs/
output/
# scratch a figure tool leaves beside its work
_render-work/
figures-work/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# uv / venv
.venv/

# Local agent permissions: names the MCP servers of THIS machine (including a
# corporate one), so it is environment config, not project content. The reusable
# part of .claude/ — the reviewer agents — stays tracked.
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# frontend (SPEC-UI): deps and build output
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/test-results/
web/playwright-report/

# IDE scratch
*.code-workspace

# Internal documents (specs, design write-ups, roadmap, progress log) live in docs/ and
# the repository is public, so they are excluded by the allow-list above rather than by a
# rule of their own. README's illustrations are in assets/, which IS allowed, so nothing
# published needs an exception.
